data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":324,"item_id":"fc_08250c39c7e1fa30016ae21b3d47208191afdf365eaef34841","output_index":0,"arguments":"{\"pointer\":\"/checks/complete_target_and_representations\",\"coverage\":\"assessed\",\"judgment\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"All parameters, all six hypotheses, positive-time domains and every target clause match under the verified coordinate/total-extension interpretation. Fin n indexes the n standard coordinate directions; EuclideanSpace gives the target's squared Euclidean norms, while coordinate product volume is the source's explicitly specified Lebesgue measure. Equivalent finite-dimensional domain norms do not change the differential or compactness. Since wDomain is open, arbitrary extension outside positive times and restriction preserve every derivative used, including second derivatives and the derivative of the energy. Integrability and DifferentiableAt are explicit conjuncts, so neither the totalized integral nor deriv can hide a missing finiteness/differentiability claim. The whole-space integral has exactly the source normalization. Equality at arbitrary positive a,b is retained, with no constraint at zero. Relevant local definitions have no hidden proof-field assumptions; wNice/wGeometry/wLocal facts are internally established in T004–T005. Actual derivative conversions (T003) and measure-preserving coordinate-splitting/insertion conversions (T010–T011) are present in checked code, rather than merely asserted in the author's equivalence note.\",\"locations\":[\"/scope\",\"/endpoints\",\"/mechanical_summary\",\"/scope/full_target\",\"/scope/parameters\",\"/scope/hypotheses\",\"/endpoints/P/source\",\"/endpoints/P/actual\",\"/endpoints/P/correspondence\",\"/documents/0\",\"/documents/2\"]}}"}

